<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <title>Malformed Scripts</title>
</head>

<body>
    <h1>Malformed script sections</h1>
    <p>
        Each section below is malformed. Instead of a blank page or a generic 500,
        the error is embedded directly in the page as a <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> block,
        and the surrounding HTML still renders.
    </p>

    <h2>Syntax error</h2>
    <rhp>function(</rhp>

    <h2>Runtime error</h2>
    <rhp>throw new Error('boom')</rhp>

    <h2>Error between valid sections</h2>
    <rhp>write('before -')</rhp>
    <rhp>const x = missing.fn()</rhp>
    <rhp>write(' - after')</rhp>

</body>

</html>
